USE NS re DB kb;
-- ============================================================================
-- 36g (2026-06-15): FRAME-ALIGNED BYTE+PIXEL DIFF of the HUD name garble.
-- Definitive verdict from the captured vframe 86530 (_hud_cap_namegap: wire
-- VRAM/PVR prefix + HUDQ tail) rendered through the REAL client pvr2 path.
-- Supersedes the bowtie-re-tile framing (36f) AND the stale-VRAM framing (9e78f3223)
-- for the NAME garble specifically. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_namegap_framealigned_diff_2026_06_15 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/_hud_cap_namegap (vframe 86530, 114 HudQuads). Diff via render_hudq.mjs through web/webgpu/pvr2-renderer.mjs + texture-manager.mjs against the SHIPPED wire prefix (vram_prefix.bin 8MB, pvr_prefix.bin 32KB).',
  note='QUAD INVENTORY: 114 HudQuads = 52 ParaType-4 polys (pcw bits29-31==4) + 62 ParaType-5 sprites (pcw=a2000009). The 62 para5 sprites are indices 41..102; they sample 62 SEPARATE tiny fmt=5 PAL4 tiles 0x415400..0x41Cxxx (tcw 2a282a80++0x40). STATE DIFF: the para5 sprite VRAM IS populated in the shipped prefix (0x415400=897/2048, 0x415c00=1014/2048, 0x417000=1015/2048 nonzero bytes) -> texels present, NOT a stale/empty VRAM bank. TA/PIXEL DIFF (the real bug): rendered para4-only vs para5-only through the verbatim client path: (a) para4-ONLY at identity[0,1,2,3] = COMPLETELY CLEAN: portraits upright, red bars clean, AND the character NAMES render LEGIBLY ("INEL"=SENTINEL readable) -- the names are drawn by the para4/para2 FONT polys at 0x4df000(fmt1)/0x4e7000(fmt2)/0x47b800(fmt2), NOT by the para5 sprites. (b) para5-ONLY = PURE GARBAGE: a blue/teal diagonal wedge streak + scattered yellow/purple fragments, NO letters at ANY strip order. THE STREAK IS THE para5 LAYER. So the user-visible name "fuzz" = the legible para4 names being overdrawn/polluted by the para5 streak composited on top.';

UPSERT finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile SET
  statement='ROOT CAUSE of the HUD name garble = the SERVER capture of the ParaType-5 sprite verts is GARBAGE for ~2/3 of sprites, NOT a client triangulation/re-tile bug and NOT a VRAM/decode bug. EVIDENCE (frame-aligned, source:hud_namegap_framealigned_diff_2026_06_15): (1) The plane-conformance test (flycast CaclulateSpritePlane fixed assignment A=cv2,B=cv3,C=cv1,P=cv0; cv0 MUST equal the plane-interp of cv1/2/3) holds for only 10/32 testable para5 sprites (err<0.01). If collectHudQuads captured flycast`s clean expanded [P,C,A,B] this would be ~32/32. So for ~22/32 sprites the captured 4 verts are NOT the 4 contiguous expansion verts -- they are mixed verts from adjacent glyphs. (2) Geometric perimeter-validity of the captured array order under the client strip is order-independent broken: identity 29/62, prod[0,1,3,2] 16/62, gitwc-sprite[2,3,1,0] 22/62, per-quad centroid-FAN 47/62 -- NO order makes them clean because the INPUT verts are wrong, and the FAN still fails large visible quads (idx55 area=156px). (3) Rendering para5-only = the blue streak with no letters at any order; rendering para4-only = clean legible names. WHY THE CAPTURE FAILS: collectHudQuads (oracle_hook.cpp L3037-3047) reads the para5 sprites via the seen==0 path = rc.verts[pp.first..pp.first+count] DIRECTLY, on the assumption pp.first is the sprite`s 4 contiguous AppendSpriteVertexA/B expansion verts. In the AUTOSORT-TRANSLUCENT HUD pass this assumption is FALSE: ta_util.cpp sortTriangles re-sorts/merges the tr list so pp.first is no longer the contiguous expansion base for sprites -> the 4 read verts straddle two glyphs. (Exactly the failure mode the comment at L3018-3024 tried to AVOID for the rc.idx path, but the seen==0 rc.verts-direct fallback hits the SAME re-sort.) THE FIX (server, preferred): in collectHudQuads, for isSpritePara, do NOT trust pp.first into the post-sort rc.verts; capture the sprite`s 4 verts from the PRE-SORT expansion (read them at AppendSpriteVertexA/B time, or index the un-permuted expansion base), OR capture the 3 raw TA_Sprite1A/1B corners + plane-vert and let the client expand. ALTERNATIVE (client, ship-now mitigation): since the para4/para2 FONT polys ALREADY render the names legibly and the para5 sprites contribute ONLY garbage, SUPPRESS ParaType-5 quads in buildHudTA (the existing _hudRenderMode=`no-sprites` path) -> names clean immediately, zero server change. This is the validated quick fix; the server capture fix is the correct long-term path if the para5 sprites carry distinct art (they appear to be a redundant name layer in this frame).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile->cites->source:hud_namegap_framealigned_diff_2026_06_15;
RELATE finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile->about->finding:hud_sprite_paratype5_client_recipe;
RELATE finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile->cites->source:replica_collectHudQuads;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36g FIX IMPLEMENTED (2026-06-15, feat/render-replica-live, commit 6dab29708):
-- SERVER-side expansion-time capture. Supersedes the prior "sortTriangles permutes
-- pp.first" MECHANISM (that hypothesis is REFUTED by the flycast source: ta_util.cpp
-- sortTriangles 66-190 appends to rc.idx/sortedTriangles only and does NOT mutate
-- pp.first/pp.count; the para5 HUD sprites are ListType=2 Translucent (pcw a2000009,
-- bits24-26=2) so on the autosort path makeIndex is NOT run on the tr list either).
-- The empirical garbage is REAL regardless of the attributed mechanism, so the fix
-- bypasses the post-parse rc.verts entirely.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_para5_expansion_capture_fix_2026_06_15 SET kind='code',
  ref='flycast core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp AppendSpriteVertexA/B (1047-1153) + CaclulateSpritePlane (1075-1122); ta_util.cpp sortTriangles (66-190) + makeIndex/makePrimRestartIndex (368-537); maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads + mc_oracle_spriteVert{Reset,Push}; ta_vtx.cpp ta_parse_vdrc reset hook + AppendSpriteVertexB push hook.',
  note='OPTION (a) implemented. At AppendSpriteVertexB (right after CaclulateSpritePlane(cv) closes cv0 as the parallelogram 4th corner P=B+C-A), stash the 4 CLOSED expansion verts cv[0..3]=[P,C,A,B] (x,y,u,v,col) into a per-parse side table (mc_oracle_spriteVertPush), reset each parse in ta_parse_vdrc (mc_oracle_spriteVertReset). collectHudQuads, for isSpritePara ((pcw>>29)&7==5), consumes the side table by running ORDINAL (spriteOrd++) instead of reading rc.verts[pp.first..]. Ordinal match is EXACT because the autosort-translucent tr PolyParam vector preserves TA submission order (sortTriangles permutes rc.idx only; sortPolyParams runs only under PerStripSorting=OFF headless, and MVC2 is not Naomi2). Non-sprite polys keep the existing rc.idx/rc.verts walk. NO WIRE CHANGE (96-byte HudQuad; client unchanged). Gated MAPLECAST_HUD_TA (push early-returns when unarmed → zero prod cost). Built MAPLECAST_HEADLESS=ON on dev box 65.109.77.178, binary md5 ac398c48cc19825f69a6911eb7ea113f, staged /home/tris/flycast-36g-staged (chmod +x). NOT deployed (user coordinates prod 149.28.44.118).';

UPSERT finding:hud_para5_expansion_capture_fix SET
  statement='FIX for finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile. Capture the ParaType-5 sprite corners at EXPANSION time (AppendSpriteVertexB, post-CaclulateSpritePlane) into an ordinal side table consumed by collectHudQuads, instead of reading the post-parse rc.verts[pp.first..]. VERIFICATION (plane-conformance test = the captured cv0 must equal the parallelogram closure of A=cv2,B=cv3,C=cv1 i.e. P=B+C-A, tol 1.0px; harness tools/render-replica-poc/hud_plane_conformance.mjs): (1) EMPIRICAL BASELINE on the LIVE prod replica-live feed (OLD binary) = 0/24 sprites pass (errs ~53px) -> the live garbage is confirmed end-to-end, even worse than the 36g 10/32 testable subset. (2) FIX-LOGIC UNIT PROOF = 32/32: the side-table path copies cv[P,C,A,B] verbatim and CaclulateSpritePlane builds cv0 = B+C-A, so the plane invariant holds BY CONSTRUCTION for every sprite. (3) A fresh live capture from the REBUILT binary on the dev box could NOT be taken: the only dev-box savestate (/home/tris/mvc2-rom-test/mvc2.state, md5 7962454a) loads OUT-OF-MATCH (0x8C289624==0 across thousands of stepped frames; mirror streams 2867 frames but collectHud/onRenderFrame never fire, no qdiag), so the in_match-gated HUD path never runs there. REMAINING GATE: run `node tools/render-replica-poc/hud_plane_conformance.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live --want-spr 24 --tol 1.0` AGAINST THE DEPLOYED FIX (or any in-match feed of the new binary) -> expect ~32/32 (up from 0/24). The pass criterion is structural-guaranteed; the live run is the confirmation.',
  status='implemented_pending_live_verify', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:hud_para5_expansion_capture_fix->fixes->finding:hud_para5_capture_is_garbage_not_retile;
RELATE finding:hud_para5_expansion_capture_fix->cites->source:hud_para5_expansion_capture_fix_2026_06_15;
